<p>Peru’s National Elections Board confirmed on Sunday that conservative Keiko Fujimori and leftist Roberto Sánchez will compete in a June 7 presidential runoff after no candidate won more than half of valid votes in the April 12 first round. The final count put Fujimori first with between about 17.1% and 17.19% of the vote and Sánchez second with 12.03%, narrowly ahead of ultraconservative Rafael López Aliaga, who received about 11.9%. The confirmation followed a prolonged count after delays in election materials, especially in Lima, disrupted the first-round vote, forcing some polling places to extend voting or reopen the next day. Fujimori, 50, is a congresswoman, Popular Force candidate and daughter of the late former President Alberto Fujimori; Sánchez is a Juntos por el Perú candidate and former foreign trade minister under former President Pedro Castillo.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/UgzM1mfK7jZSDkFU6aRrNiUBJwBZC_HmV-iS4E3ZhrBEEDlr0o3fZ34y8jmBHwPxgKFC0zc6W0d-18bhy0Kf1KY1NlK-qeFZ92oQhMENO0Pf7gPdfHb9SvGL6jW63Gcws6Y_bnPMCuR6oNhU8J3euW1lhAcSS63BQGgkhcYvvyNmGgmeBhkaI02v13gpLiEBBYKx40TN6f5fd34' alt='Keiko Fujimori, the leader of the Popular Force Party, at a campaign rally last month in Lima, Peru.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Narrow margin: Fujimori received about 2.88 million votes, Sánchez about 2.02 million and López Aliaga about 1.99 million, leaving Sánchez ahead of third place by 21,209 votes.</li><li>Fragmented vote: More than 70% of voters chose neither runoff candidate in the first round, leaving both campaigns to seek support beyond their original bases.</li><li>Crowded field: The April 12 election included more than 30 candidates, with some sources saying Fujimori and Sánchez beat 33 other contenders.</li><li>Voting disruption: Delays in the delivery of election materials kept more than 50,000 people from voting on schedule, ORF reported.</li><li>2021 parallel: Fujimori previously faced Pedro Castillo in the 2021 second-round race, according to Diario Libre.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>National Elections Board: JNE President Roberto Burneo formally proclaimed Fujimori and Sánchez the two candidates with the highest relative vote totals, clearing the way for the runoff. (<a href='https://www.diariolibre.com/actualidad/nacional/2026/05/17/autoridad-electoral-oficializa-balotaje-fujimori-y-sanchez-en-peru/3536404'>Diario Libre</a>)</li><li>Peru’s top electoral authority: The electoral authority pledged to correct flaws that delayed first-round results before Peru holds the June 7 runoff. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/peru-electoral-body-pledges-to-fix-voting-flaws-ahead-of-june-presidential-runoff'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>European Union observers: The EU observation mission cited grave deficiencies in the first round but did not challenge the validity of the election. (<a href='https://www.diariolibre.com/actualidad/nacional/2026/05/17/autoridad-electoral-oficializa-balotaje-fujimori-y-sanchez-en-peru/3536404'>Diario Libre</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/peru-electoral-body-pledges-to-fix-voting-flaws-ahead-of-june-presidential-runoff'>Peru electoral body pledges to fix voting &#x27;flaws&#x27; ahead of June presidential runoff</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/world/americas/peru-runoff-election.html'>Runoff in Peru Offers Two Starkly Differing Visions for the Nation</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/perus-electoral-board-confirms-june-7-presidential-runoff-133050906'>Peru&#x27;s electoral board confirms June 7 presidential runoff with Fujimori and Sánchez</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/17/left-wing-candidate-roberto-sanchez-advances-to-presidential-runoff-in-peru_6753533_4.html'>Left-wing candidate Roberto Sanchez advances to presidential runoff in Peru</a> - lemonde.fr</